# Measured with `make mutate-all` (gremlins over the whole module):
#
#   mutants_total 998 · killed 982 · LIVED 16 · not_covered 83 · timed_out 9
#   test efficacy 98.40% · mutator coverage 92.32%
#
# The 16 survivors are allowlisted. Six entries were retired because their mutants
# no longer exist or are now KILLED (the relativeTime bounds, the toast expiry
# guard and the three `make` capacity hints, whose `+N` was removed from the code),
# four entries were added for mutants the previous run did not report, and one real
# gap was closed with a test (the detail.go list clip widths).
#
# CAREFUL with `TIMED OUT`: it does not go into `mutants_total` and the gate only
# looks at `LIVED`, so a run with untested mutants can report 100% efficacy. See
# MUTATE_TIMEOUT_COEFFICIENT in the Makefile.
#
# The two classes you have to decide on, which repeated across the whole repo:
#
#   1. Real test gap -> cover it with a test. Examples: the exact value of a
#      bound, the width a cell composes, how a budget is split.
#   2. Mutation that is an IDENTITY by construction -> no test can kill it,
#      because there is no bug to kill. There the honest move is NOT to
#      allowlist it: it is to remove the mutated site (rewrite the guard, delete
#      it if it was useless) or, if the shape of the code demands it, allowlist
#      it with the demonstration.
#
# Every entry below carries that demonstration. The order is by file.
